  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«cứ… là…»: as soon as…, whenever…",
     "texto": [
      "**Cứ + A + là + B** = as long as A happens, B happens; each time A, B. It is the most spoken way to express a habit: «**Cứ** nghe nhạc này **là** tớ buồn ngủ» = just hearing this music and I get sleepy. «**Cứ** đến thứ hai **là** chán» = every Monday I'm fed up.",
      "**Cứ** + verb (without «là») = to keep on doing it, to just do it: «**Cứ** nói đi» = just talk. «Nó **cứ** cười» = it keeps on laughing."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How young people talk and write",
     "texto": [
      "This **is not for use in an exam**, but you'll see it in every chat. Fairly established words:",
      "**xịn** = top quality, the good ones. **đỉnh** = the best, top. **chất** = stylish. **chán** = a drag. **bó tay** = I give up, nobody can beat that.",
      "**chém gió** = to brag, to talk nonsense. **thả thính** = to flirt, to make a move. **sống ảo** = to live for social media. **trẻ trâu** = a brat. **gấu** = boyfriend or girlfriend. **ế** = single.",
      "In messages everything gets shortened: **ko / k** = không · **dc / đc** = được · **j** = gì · **r** = rồi · **bt** = bình thường / biết · **ng** = người · **mk** = mình · **ntn** = như thế nào.",
      "And English gets mixed in: **ok**, **check**, **deadline**, **sale**.",
      "Rule: understand it all, use it only with people of your own age whom you trust, and never in formal writing."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
